---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: sdk-source-of-record-governance
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  The SDK is the single-source-of-record home: schemas/v1 (enums, views, registries, axis cards)
  generate every downstream projection (TS types, Rust constants, ordinal comparators). The
  recurring drift this directory breeds is hand-authored vocabulary — a value typed here instead
  of generated from here is how five reach vocabularies diverged. Authored at inject/measure tier
  by agent self-grant per the governance escalation ladder (2026-07-23 discipline-1 slice):
  enforcement-class escalation to ask/deny is reserved to operator ratification.
rules:
  - id: generated-is-projection
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*generated*" }
    why: >
      Files under a generated path are projections — the source of record is the schema or card
      that generates them (schemas/v1 + codegen scripts). Hand-edits here re-drift on the next
      codegen run. Edit the source, re-run codegen (pnpm run schema:codegen:ts / cargo test
      export_bindings), and commit source + projection together.
  - id: new-vocabulary-declares-source
    class: inject
    when: { write: "schemas/v1/enums/*.schema.json", new: true }
    why: >
      A new closed vocabulary must state "Source of truth:" in its description (schema_contract
      asserts this), decide its tier deliberately (_dna only via a deliberate DNA-lineage event),
      and consider an axis card in registries/axes/ when the vocabulary is an orthogonal
      coordinate (reach/locality/custody/epistemic pattern). Drift law: exactly ONE generative
      source-of-record per vocabulary; every other appearance is generated or an explicit re-export.
---

# elohim/sdk — source-of-record governance

This subtree is where vocabularies are BORN; the rules above keep them born-governed
(advisory tier — they inform, never block). The reach reconciliation (slices 1-3) and the
ontology keel (2026-07-23) are the case law: hand-typed vocabulary values outside a declared
source-of-record are the recurring defect class here.
